WEBVTT

1
00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:26.800
<v Circuit>I built three systems for a sample software company.

2
00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:32.200
<v Circuit>One sorts new leads and books demos.

3
00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:37.600
<v Circuit>One follows up failed card payments.

4
00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:45.600
<v Circuit>One is an AI helper that hands the rest to a person.

5
00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:51.700
<v Circuit>Then I built the whole set on four tools.

6
00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:59.900
<v Circuit>Four complete builds of the same job.

7
00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:08.900
<v Circuit>They all did the job. Next question: how do they hold up?

8
00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:18.200
<v Flow>Now I try to break every one of them.

9
00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:27.200
<v Flow>Same break tests, run on every build.

10
00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:39.000
<v Flow>Eight requirements and sixteen details per build.

11
00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:45.700
<v Circuit>Here is what the testing showed.

12
00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:54.500
<v Circuit>A new lead gets a first text in about 10 seconds on n8n.

13
00:01:54.500 --> 00:02:01.800
<v Circuit>On Make, the whole run took under 3 seconds.

14
00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:09.500
<v Flow>On trick questions, Make got 12 of 12.

15
00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:16.600
<v Flow>Zapier got 8 of 12, answering four it should have passed.

16
00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:22.800
<v Circuit>n8n runs on its own server for $5.35 a month.

17
00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:28.500
<v Circuit>Testing found a real problem on Make, and I fixed it.

18
00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:32.000
<v Circuit>Let's recap what happened.
